  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "A die is rolled five times. Find the probability that:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q17-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the first two rolls are sixes, and the next three are not",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{125}{7776}$",
          "worked": "The order is specified, so multiply the independent probabilities.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(SSFFF)&=\\left(\\frac16\\right)^2\\left(\\frac56\\right)^3\\\\\\Pr(SSFFF)&=\\frac{125}{7776}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q17-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "exactly two of the rolls are sixes, and the other three are not.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{625}{3888}$",
          "worked": "Let $X$ count sixes. There are $\\binom52$ possible placements of the two sixes.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(X=2)&=\\binom52\\left(\\frac16\\right)^2\\left(\\frac56\\right)^3\\\\\\Pr(X=2)&=10\\times\\frac{125}{7776}\\\\\\Pr(X=2)&=\\frac{625}{3888}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      }
    ]
  },
